Z||000004||Haagster||09-03-2001||09:41 AM||||Playing tag with a big truck???  What company was he from?  Any idea?  If so, call his/her company safety department (I can probably get you a phone number) and file a complaint.  He/she may or may not report the incident to the company, but if you do...  At least my company would have one less driver on the road (and the record would follow to the next company that hired the clown as a driver).  CDL drivers are supposed to be professional, it's clowns like that who give drivers a bad name on the road.  [as I step down from my soap box]<P>BTW:  Was the car damaged???  Guaranteed law suit...  Otherwise, it's just "road rage".<P>If you're ever in HBG area, let us know you are coming (not always practical, but...)<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Signature_4.jpg"> ||||reg||6
Z||000005||Spektrum-87GT||09-03-2001||12:05 PM||||i had something like that happen once, heres what i did: slowed down a lot, ~25mph, and then slammed on the brakes! of course.. i was in a beat up cherokee... that i couldnt sell for more than 2k but i could get over 6k from the trucks insurance company! he backed way off after that. would never try it in a fiero though!||||reg||1
